# UI Design System (OfficeFlow)

Dark-first, Apple-like: simple, premium, precise. Hierarchy via typography and spacing — not color noise or card stacks.

When this rule is attached / always on: follow it for all frontend UI work. Prefer existing tokens (`--of-*`, `of-*` classes) over one-off styles.

## Direction

- Feel: professional, premium, precise, modern, calm
- Product UI (app), not marketing landing — restraint over spectacle
- References: Apple.com hero / mega-menu / bag (typography, hairlines, sparse accent)
- Contrast first: canvas / surface / field / ink must stay clearly separated (avoid mid-gray mud)

## Color (dark first)

Brand DNA stays `#715A5A` (soft fills). UI uses lifted variants for readability.

| Role | Token / HEX | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Background | `--of-bg` `#2A2830` | App canvas (deeper than surfaces) |
| Surface / tiles | `--of-bg-solid` `#44444E` | Panels, sheets, solid bars |
| Elevated | `--of-bg-elevated` `rgba(68,68,78,0.94)` | Blurred toolbar / material |
| Field | `--of-bg-field` `#37353E` | Inputs (recessed into surface) |
| Ink | `--of-ink` `#E8EDEB` | Primary text / icons |
| Ink muted | `--of-ink-secondary` `#B4BBBA` | Meta, inactive nav |
| Ink tertiary | `#9AA19F` | Captions only |
| Brand DNA | `#715A5A` | Soft backgrounds (`brand-soft`), identity |
| Brand fill | `--of-brand` / `brand-600` `#8B6E6E` | Primary CTA, active nav pill |
| Brand active/text | `brand-700` `#C9A8A8` | Text links, focus ring, selected map |
| On accent | `--of-on-brand` `#F7F4F4` | Text on primary button |
| Accent soft | `--of-brand-soft` `rgba(113,90,90,0.28)` | Focus ring soft fill |
| Separator | `rgba(232,237,235,0.18)` | Hairlines |
| Danger | `#E08A8A` | Errors / destructive |
| Success | soft brand-adjacent, not loud green SaaS |

Light mode (fallback): bg `#F3F2F4`, surface `#FFFFFF`, field `#E9E8EB`, ink `#2A282E`, brand fill `#8B6E6E`.

Do not invent new accent hues. Map tiles use ink/brand soft tones — not pastel SaaS greens/blues. Space tiles must read lighter than the map floor.

## Typography

Use system SF stack (do not host SF Pro as a webfont):

```css
font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "SF Pro Text", "SF Pro Display",
  "Segoe UI", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
```

| Style | Size | Weight | Tracking |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Display | 28–32px | 600 | -0.02em |
| Title | 20–22px | 600 | -0.015em |
| Body | 15px | 400 | 0 |
| Caption / label | 12–13px | 500 | ~0.01em |

Prefer `of-display`, `of-title`, `of-body`, `of-caption`, `of-label`. Importance = size/weight, not extra color.

## Shape & controls (CTA)

- **App primary / secondary buttons:** `border-radius: 12px` (`rounded-control`)
- **Nav chips only:** pill `980px` (`rounded-pill` / `of-nav-pill`)
- Primary fill: `#8B6E6E` + on-brand text
- Secondary: ghost / fill (`--of-fill`)
- Active nav: `bg-brand-600` + `on-brand` (not dark DNA `#715A5A` on dark canvas)
- Text actions: `text-brand-700` (`#C9A8A8` in dark)

## Layout & surfaces

- One job per section; generous spacing; avoid nested cards
- Surfaces: `#44444E` + hairline — **no multi-layer drop shadows**
- Material/toolbar: light blur OK; do not glassmorph everything
- Overlays: scrim + blur
- Dividers: hairlines with enough alpha to stay visible

## Motion

- Press feedback: `scale(0.97)` ~120ms ease-out
- Sheets/drawers: existing drawer curve
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`

## Anti-patterns

- Purple/indigo gradients, glow, neon
- Inter/Roboto as brand font
- Cards everywhere; emoji in chrome
- Using DNA `#715A5A` as the only interactive fill on dark (too muddy)
- Flat mid-gray stack (bg ≈ surface ≈ field ≈ muted text)

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="rounded-2xl bg-purple-600 shadow-xl shadow-purple-500/30">…

// ✅ GOOD
<button className="of-btn-primary">Confirm</button>
<section className="of-surface">…</section>
```

## Implementation notes

- Source of truth: `frontend/src/index.css` + `frontend/tailwind.config.js`
- Change tokens first, then components — no ad-hoc HEX in feature TSX
- This rule is always applied (`alwaysApply: true`); also linked from `.cursorrules`
